# Spark DS — Extending the System

When the design system does not cover a need, follow this order. Do not skip steps.

## 1. Search first

- Grep `css/tokens.css` for related `--semantic-*` names.
- Read foundation and component pages for composable patterns.

## 2. Compose before creating

- Prefer existing semantic tokens combined in new CSS.
- Match patterns from documented components (Button is the reference for states, focus, sizes).

## 3. Add tokens at the correct tier

| Need | Add to |
|------|--------|
| New raw color or size | `--primitive-*` in `tokens.css` only |
| Reusable meaning (error text, card border) | `--semantic-*` |
| Single component scope (button hover) | `--semantic-{component}-*` |

Never reference `--primitive-*` from React component CSS.

## 4. Document the change

In the same change set:

- Update `tokens.css`
- Update the relevant foundation or component HTML page
- Link new components from `index.html`
- Update the Spark Figma library (`fileKey`: `KYq9ka9Hg16HdfzR4gMoMH`) using Figma MCP and the `figma-generate-library` skill

## 5. Add or update Cursor rules

When a component stabilizes, add props and usage to `spark-ds-react-components.mdc`.

## When blocked

If requirements conflict with Spark DS or no token fits, stop and ask. Do not ship hardcoded values as a permanent solution.
